1
00:04:57,857 --> 00:05:03,857
Everybody loved him... Everybody disappeared. The journey is everything.

2
00:09:55,714 --> 00:10:01,714
Jerry Maguire is a comedy, drama, romance film directed by Cameron Crowe.

3
00:14:53,571 --> 00:14:59,571
Jerry Maguire used to be a typical sports agent: willing to do just about anything he could to get
the biggest possible contracts for his clients, plus a nice commission for himself.

4
00:19:51,428 --> 00:19:57,428
Then, one day, he suddenly has second thoughts about what he's really doing.

5
00:24:49,285 --> 00:24:55,285
When he voices these doubts, he ends up losing his job and all of his
clients, save Rod Tidwell, an egomaniacal football player.

6
00:29:47,142 --> 00:29:53,142
Jerry Maguire, played by Tom Cruise.

7
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:51,000
Dorothy Boyd, played by Renée Zellweger.

8
00:39:42,857 --> 00:39:48,857
Rod Tidwell, played by Cuba Gooding Jr..

9
00:44:40,714 --> 00:44:46,714
Avery Bishop, played by Kelly Preston.

10
00:49:38,571 --> 00:49:44,571
Frank Cushman, played by Jerry O'Connell.

11
00:54:36,428 --> 00:54:42,428
Bob Sugar, played by Jay Mohr.

12
00:59:34,285 --> 00:59:40,285
Jerry Maguire is a 1996 American sports romantic comedy
film written and directed by Cameron Crowe.

13
01:04:32,142 --> 01:04:38,142
It was produced by Crowe and James L.

14
01:09:30,000 --> 01:09:36,000
Brooks, respectively for Vinyl Films and Gracie Films and distributed by
Sony Pictures Releasing under the TriStar Pictures label.

15
01:14:27,857 --> 01:14:33,857
It stars Tom Cruise as the titular sports agent character, alongside Cuba Gooding Jr., Renée
Zellweger, Kelly Preston, Jerry O'Connell, Jay Mohr, Bonnie Hunt and Regina King.

16
01:19:25,714 --> 01:19:31,714
It was released in North American theaters on December 13, 1996.

17
01:24:23,571 --> 01:24:29,571
Jerry Maguire was inspired by an experience with the sports agent Leigh Steinberg, a technical consultant for the film and his client,
Tim McDonald (who makes a cameo appearance in this film) during the 1993 NFL season when free agency was introduced.

18
01:29:21,428 --> 01:29:27,428
The film was also partly inspired by a 28-page memo written
at Disney in 1991 by Jeffrey Katzenberg.

19
01:34:19,285 --> 01:34:25,285
Jerry Maguire received positive reviews for its performances and screenplay.

20
01:39:17,142 --> 01:39:23,142
It grossed more than $273 million worldwide against its $50 million budget.

21
01:44:14,999 --> 01:44:20,999
It was the ninth-highest-grossing film of 1996.

22
01:49:12,857 --> 01:49:18,857
It was nominated for five Academy Awards, including Best Picture
and Best Actor for Cruise, with Cuba Gooding Jr.

23
01:54:10,714 --> 01:54:16,714
winning Best Supporting Actor, in addition to the Screen
Actors Guild Award in the same category.

24
01:59:08,571 --> 01:59:14,571
Cruise won the Golden Globe Award for Best Actor in a
Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy.

25
02:04:06,428 --> 02:04:12,428
Jerry Maguire gained a cult following and has spawned several catchphrases into popular
culture, such as "you had me at 'hello'", "you complete me" and "show me the money".

26
02:09:04,285 --> 02:09:10,285
The film explores themes of career, sports, stadium,
american football, single mother.

27
02:14:02,142 --> 02:14:08,142
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
